---
---
<section id="philosophy" class="py-24 border-t border-white/5 relative">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-400 mb-3">Core Philosophy</h2>
      <h3 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-4">
        The Art of "Hozotsugi" (ほぞ継ぎ)
      </h3>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Named after traditional Japanese joinery — joining distinct structural components into a single seamless whole without unnecessary nails or adhesive.
        Hozo unites React Native, the Semantic Web, Tailwind CSS, and strict accessibility.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Pillar 1 -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-2xl glass-panel relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-indigo-500/30 transition-all">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-indigo-400 font-bold text-lg mb-6 group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform">
          01
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          Existing Source First
        </h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          No mandatory rewrite or foreign DSL. Existing React Native code importing from <code class="text-slate-300">react-native</code> is parsed directly. Adopt Hozo incrementally without breaking your current workflow.
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5 text-xs font-mono text-slate-300">
          <span class="text-indigo-300">import</span> &#123; View, Text &#125; <span class="text-indigo-300">from</span> <span class="text-emerald-300">'react-native'</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Pillar 2 -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-2xl glass-panel relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-sky-500/30 transition-all">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-sky-500/10 border border-sky-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-sky-400 font-bold text-lg mb-6 group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform">
          02
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          Golden Path for New Projects
        </h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <code class="text-slate-300">@hozo/core</code> provides canonical and semantic primitives (<code class="text-slate-300">Heading</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">Paragraph</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">Section</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">Button</code>) for the fastest, most accessible path from day one.
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5 text-xs font-mono text-slate-300">
          <span class="text-sky-300">import</span> &#123; Heading, Button &#125; <span class="text-sky-300">from</span> <span class="text-emerald-300">'@hozo/core'</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Pillar 3 -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-2xl glass-panel relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-emerald-500/30 transition-all">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400 font-bold text-lg mb-6 group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform">
          03
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          Compile What You Can, Fall Back Gracefully
        </h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          100% static compilation is never assumed. Hozo compiles static styles to real CSS, compiles conditionals to booleans, and falls back to cached runtime resolution when truly dynamic.
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5 text-xs font-mono text-slate-300 text-emerald-400">
          Static (0ms) &rarr; Structural (Branching) &rarr; Dynamic fallback
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Pillar 4 -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-2xl glass-panel relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-amber-500/30 transition-all">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-amber-400 font-bold text-lg mb-6 group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform">
          04
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          Accessibility is Not Optional
        </h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          ARIA is the first-class vocabulary. The compiler validates roles and missing attributes using <code class="text-slate-300">aria-query</code>. Full focus trapping, roving tabindexes, and dialog patterns via <code class="text-slate-300">@hozo/a11y</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5 text-xs font-mono text-amber-400">
          Compile-time diagnostics + W3C ARIA specs
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
